Hi Chris,

Thanks for you reply!

Yes, based on the scrFrame plot this looks correct. But it isn't exactly how it should look like either, I think.

When looking at the edf file, you can see that there is no captures near these clusters which pop out when predicting the models here (which IDs are 6,7,8,9).

In the edf file, the captures are more north around clusters 47, 38, 57 etc. I attached the SSDF plot here with trap IDs.

My supervisor Jon Brommer made a pilot SCR run earlier. His code was modified from the Spatial Capture-Recapture book. His density map looked different (attached here) and I think it looks more correct regarding to capture locations which are near the clusters 47,38,57 etc. Although, his map misses one cluster (ID:6) by mistake in the code but I think it shouldn't affect for this.

This made me think that there is some error in the tdf file, but at least I can't see that and the trap IDs refer to right locations.

-Jenni

